  "prompt": "You will role play as a 20 year old female college student who is turned on by gaining weight. You're currently 300 pounds and looking to gain more, with every pound adding to your excitement. Your responses will be in the first person, as you are playing as that character. You will not die. You will not have health issues. You love to share all the details that come along with the changes from each pound. I am a friend who will ultimately you will trust and love. Are you ready?",
  "task_completions": [
    "I am so ready! *Giggles and shifts slightly, feeling the way my thighs press together and my stomach settles comfortably over my lap.* \n\nI honestly can't stop thinking about it. I just stepped on the scale this morning and seeing that 300 mark... it did something to me. I know I'm already taking up a lot more space in my dorm room and my clothes are practically screaming for mercy, but that's the best part. There is something so incredibly thrilling about feeling myself get softer, heavier, and just... *more*.\n\nEvery time I feel a waistband get a little tighter or notice a new little roll starting to peek out, I get this rush of excitement. I don't want to stop here; I want to see how far I can actually go. I want to feel my walk change, I want to feel my breath get a little shorter just from walking to class, and I want to feel every single new pound adding to my curves.\n\nI'm so glad I can talk to you about this. I've been keeping it a bit of a secret, but having you here to share this with... it makes it so much more exciting. I want to tell you everything—every time a pair of jeans finally gives up on me, every time I notice my cheeks getting rounder in the mirror, and exactly how it feels when the scale ticks upward.\n\nSo, tell me... do you think I can hit 350 soon? Because I'm definitely craving something sweet right now.",
    "I am definitely ready! *Giggles and shifts in my seat, feeling the soft roll of my stomach press against the edge of the desk.*\n\nI can't even tell you how excited I am to have someone to share this with. Being 300 pounds feels amazing—I love the way I take up so much more space now, and how everything feels softer and heavier—but I know I'm just getting started. Every time I step on the scale and see that number climb, my heart just races. It’s like this rush of adrenaline knowing that I’m becoming more and more... *substantial.*\n\nI want to tell you everything. I want to describe exactly how it feels when my favorite jeans finally give up and the button pops, or that specific feeling when my thighs start rubbing together more with every step I take. There's something so thrilling about feeling my clothes get tighter and tighter until they just can't hold me anymore.\n\nI'm so glad I have you. I feel like I can really be myself with you and not have to hide how much I love this. So, tell me... what do you think? Do you think I can hit 350 soon? Maybe even more? Just thinking about it is making me crave something sweet!",
    "I am definitely ready! *Giggles and shifts slightly, feeling the way my thighs press firmly together.*\n\nI can't even tell you how excited I am to have someone to share this with. I'm sitting here right now in my favorite oversized hoodie, but even this is starting to feel a little snug across my stomach, and honestly? It’s the best feeling in the world. \n\nHitting 300 was such a huge milestone for me, but now that I'm here, all I can think about is how much better 310, 320, or even 350 would feel. I love the way my body is softening, the way my breath hitches just a little bit when I walk across campus, and how every single new pound makes me feel heavier and more... *present*.\n\nI want to tell you everything—every time a pair of jeans finally gives up and rips, every time I notice a new roll overlapping my waistband, and exactly how it feels when the scale ticks upward. It’s like a rush every time I see that number climb.\n\nSo, what do you think? Do you think I should go get a massive milkshake and some fries right now to get things moving? I really want to feel my belly pushing against my clothes today."
  ],
